This crate (`symphonia-codec-als`) is a pure-Rust MPEG-4 Audio Lossless Coding (ALS) decoder. It is
licensed under the Mozilla Public License, v. 2.0, like the rest of Project Symphonia (see
`LICENSE`).

The decoder is ported from the ALS decoder of FFmpeg (https://ffmpeg.org): the bitstream and
prediction decoder (`libavcodec/alsdec.c`, Thilo Borgmann, Umair Khan, Hendrik Leppkes and
others), the block Gilbert-Moore decoder and its code tables (`libavcodec/bgmc.c`, Thilo
Borgmann), the MLZ decompressor (`libavcodec/mlz.c`, Ivan Uskov) and the software floating-point
arithmetic (`libavutil/softfloat_ieee754.h`, Michael Niedermayer). The tables in `bgmc_tables.rs`
and `tables.rs` are taken from those files. These FFmpeg files are licensed under the GNU Lesser
General Public License, version 2.1 or (at your option) any later version.
